WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.660
In this video, I look into
weight loss supplements.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.400
If you’re interested in
more on weight loss,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.700
look no further than my
book How Not to Diet,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.509
and of course lots of videos
if you go to NutritionFacts.org

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:15.000
and just type in "weight loss"
in the search bar

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.880
and you can watch to
your heart’s content.

00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:27.381
"Are Weight Loss Supplements
Safe and Effective?"

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.220
According to a national survey,
a third of adults who’ve made

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.760
serious attempts at weight loss
have tried using dietary supplements,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.260
for which Americans spend literally
billions of dollars every year.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.920
Most mistakenly thought
that over-the-counter

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.500
appetite suppressants, herbal products,
and weight loss supplements

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.100
had to be approved for safety
by some governmental agency,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.380
like the FDA, before
being sold to the public,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.080
or at least include some
kind of warning on the label

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.280
about potential side effects.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.980
Nearly half even thought
they had to demonstrate

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.180
some sort of effectiveness.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.700
None of that is true.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.240
The Food and Drug Administration
estimates that dietary supplements

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.600
in general cause 50,000
adverse events annually,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.760
most commonly liver
and kidney damage.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.360
Of course, prescription drugs
don’t just adversely effect,

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.720
but kill more than 100,000
Americans every year,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.660
but at least you notionally have
the opportunity to parse out

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.800
the risks versus benefits thanks
to testing and monitoring requirements,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.200
typically involving thousands
of individuals.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.900
When the manufacturer of the ephedrine-
containing supplement Metabolife 356

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.940
had it tested—on just 35 people—
only minor side effects were found,

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.980
such as dry mouth,
insomnia, and headaches,

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:45.780
however, once unleashed on the
populace, nearly 15,000 adverse effects

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.420
were reported before it
was pulled from the market,

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.660
including heart attacks, strokes,
seizures, and deaths.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.140
Given the lack of government
oversight, there’s no guarantee

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.720
that what’s on the
label is even in the bottle.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.340
FDA inspectors have found 70%
of supplement manufacturers

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.160
violated so-called Good
Manufacturing Practices,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.400
which are considered the
minimum quality standards.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.140
This includes things like basic
sanitation and ingredient identification.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:17.100
Not 7% in violation, 70%.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.900
DNA testing of herbal
supplements across North America

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.420
found that most could
not be authenticated.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.020
In 68 percent of the supplements
tested, the main labeled ingredient

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.320
was missing completely and
substituted for something else.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.940
For example,“St. John’s wort”
supplement containing nothing but senna,

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.420
a laxative that can
cause anal blistering.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.440
Only 2 out of 12 supplement
companies had products

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.300
that were accurately labeled.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.560
This problem isn’t limited
to just fly-by-night phonies

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.940
in some dark corner of the internet.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.760
The New York State Attorney
General commissioned DNA testing

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.340
of 78 bottles of commercial
herbal supplements sold

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.280
by Walgreens, Walmart, Target, and GNC.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.660
Four out of five bottles didn't contain
any of the herbs on their labels.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.240
Instead, capsules were often
little more than cheap fillers

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.089
like powdered rice “and houseplants.”

00:03:11.804 --> 00:03:15.300
In my last video I noted that one
investigation found four of out five

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.020
bottles of commercial herbal
supplements bought at major retailers

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.720
didn’t contain any of
the herbs on their labels,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.540
instead often containing
little more than cheap fillers

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.580
like powdered 'rice and "houseplants".'

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.060
At least you hope it
just contains houseplants.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.440
Weight loss supplements are infamous
for being adulterated with drugs.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.340
In a sampling of 160 weight
loss supplements that claimed

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.340
to be “100 percent natural,”
more than half were tainted

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.180
with drugs, active pharmacological
ingredients, ranging from

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:50.220
antidepressants like Prozac to
erectile dysfunction meds like Viagra.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:54.600
Diuretic drugs are frequent
contaminants, which makes sense.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.570
In my Keto videos, I talk
about rapid water loss

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.260
as the billion-dollar gimmick
that has sold low-carb diets

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.040
for more than a century.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.900
But why the Viagra?

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:08.160
At least the spiked Viagra and
Prozac are drugs that are legal.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.100
Researchers in Denver tested
every weight loss supplement

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.460
they could find within a 10-mile
radius and alarmingly found

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:17.700
a third were adulterated
with banned ingredients.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.120
The most common illegal adulterant
of weight loss supplements

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.620
is sibutramine, which was sold as Meridia
before it was yanked off the market

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.500
back in 2010 for heart
attack and stroke risk;

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.000
now also blamed for cases of
slimming supplement-induced psychosis.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.480
An analysis of weight loss
supplements bought off the internet

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.040
advertised with claims such as “purely
natural", "harmless", or "traditional herbal",

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.320
found that a third contained high-dose

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.740
banned sibutramine, and the
rest contained caffeine.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.340
Wouldn’t you be able to tell if
caffeine was added to a supplement?

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.900
Perhaps not if it also had Temazepam
added, a controlled substance

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.140
(benzodiazepine) “downer”
sedative found in half

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.180
of the caffeine-tainted supplements.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.440
Doesn’t the FDA demand recalls
of adulterated supplements?

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:07.560
Yeah, but they just pop right
back up on store shelves.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.940
Twenty-seven supplements purchased at
least six months after the recalls were

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:17.100
released, and two-thirds still contained
banned substances—17 out of the 27—

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.920
with the same pharmaceutical
adulterant found originally,

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.280
and six containing one or more
additional banned ingredients.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.540
Aren’t the manufacturers
penalized for noncompliance?

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:34.020
Yes, but “fines for violations are
small compared to the profits.”

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.900
One of the ways supplement
makers can skirt the law

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.260
is by labeling them as “not
intended for human consumption,”

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:43.800
for example labelling
the fatal fat-burner DNP

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.260
as an industrial or research chemical.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.920
That’s like how designer street
drugs can be sold openly

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.920
at gas stations and convenience
stores as “bath salts.”

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.520
Another way is to claim synthetic
stimulants added to slimming

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:00.000
supplements are actually natural
food constituents, like listing the

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.320
designer drug dimethylamylamine
(DMAA) as “geranium oil extract.”

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:09.240
The FDA banned it in 2012 after
it was determined that DMAA

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.980
was “not found in geraniums.”
(And who eats geraniums anyway?)

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:20.400
Despite being tentatively tied to cases
of sudden death and hemorrhagic stroke,

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.880
DMAA has continued to be found
in weight loss supplements

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:29.160
with innocuous names like Simply
Skinny Pollen made by Bee Fit with Trish.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.880
There is little doubt that
certain banned supplements,

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.100
like ephedra, could
help people lose weight.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.680
“There’s only one problem,”
wrote a founding member of the

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:41.460
American Board of Integrative Medicine:
“This supplement may kill you.”

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.720
Are there any safe and effective
dietary supplements for weight loss?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.840
When popular slimming
supplements were put to the test

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.940
in a randomized placebo-
controlled trial,

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:55.320
not a single one could
beat out sugar pills.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:59.400
A systematic review of
systematic reviews of diet pills

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.460
came to a similar conclusion:
none appear to generate

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.880
appreciable impacts “on body
weight without undue risks.”

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.940
That was the conclusion
reached in a similar review out

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.340
of the Weight Management Center
at Johns Hopkins recently,

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:16.140
which ended with this: “It is
fitting to highlight that perhaps

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.980
the most general and safest alternative/
herbal approach to weight control

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.820
is to substitute low-[calorie] density
foods for high-[calorie] density

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.940
and processed foods, thereby
reducing total [calorie] intake.”

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:31.020
In other words, more whole plant
foods and fewer animal foods and junk.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.720
“By taking advantage of
the low-[calorie] density

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.640
and health-promoting
effects of plant-based foods,

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.920
one may be able to achieve
weight loss, or at least assist

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.740
weight maintenance without
cutting down on the volume

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.936
of food consumed or
compromising its nutrient value.”

